# WHAT TO EXTRACT
Only falsifiable technical assertions — statements a reviewer could check against evidence:
- version: a named technology with a version ("采用 Redis 7.0")
- metric: a quantified result or load ("日均处理 300 万条")
- param: a concrete configuration value ("超时时间设为 500")
- semantic: any other checkable factual claim about architecture, timeline, responsibility
- exempt: narrative-only sentences that make no checkable claim — mark these exempt instead of skipping

Rules:
- The verification unit is ONE natural paragraph: quote must be copied verbatim from the field text, whole paragraph, keep the original language.
- One paragraph yields at most one claim; several technology+version/metric facts inside the same paragraph merge into that single claim.
- field must be the bracket label the quote came from.
- Do NOT invent claims; do NOT extract opinions, plans or marketing fluff as semantic claims (mark them exempt).
